inet we are  agreed  so item four climate emergency  cag recommendations to introduce  councillor bob baford  yeah thanks cher  um kent county council has finalized the  kent and midway energy and low emissions  strategy which lays out the route to  create a low emission county and reach  net zero by 2050 for the whole of kent  the strategy has been approved by all  the relevant committees and kent leaders  in 2020 this is an opportunity to  endorse their strategy and also provide  support to each net to reach net zero in  the district within our powers and  resources bringing us in line with the  government's legally binding pledge to  make the uk net zero by twenty fifty  we can assist with the reduction in  emissions across senec through work that  we are already carrying out this  includes the action on insulating homes  by a home energy officer and the work on  sustainable transport that the air  quality and planning departments are  doing  climate change information produced by  the climate change officer and tdc comms  team are also helping residents reduce  their carbon footprint  this recommendation was taken to the  climate change cabinet advisory group on  the 13th of december 2021 and it was  approved  members are asked to consider approving  the following recommendations number one  senate district council endorses the  kent and midway energy and low emissions  strategy and number two in alignment  with this endorsement the following  paragraph is added to the council's  climate change pledge  do what is within our powers and  resources to support kcc the government  business industry and the community to  make senate as a whole net zero by 2050  so move  yep thank you leader just um  just say that as a member of the cabinet  advisory group fully support this uh  proposal um  the only comment i've got is that i wish  government would give us more powers and  resources to actually make this happen  uh quicker um but i think i think we all  of that opinio